{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49120","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:53.756663+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Internal reproducer submitted in cl/985794605.","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:42:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49120#issuecomment-5772889998","id":5772889998,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49120","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABWBdPjg","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5772889998/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-22T07:42:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5772889998","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194224583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penumallas1261","id":194224583,"login":"penumallas1261","node_id":"U_kgDOC5Ohxw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penumallas1261","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"I already have a potential fix for this: https://github.com/openxla/xla/pull/49309\n\nStill needs to be reviewed.","created_at":"2026-09-23T11:46:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/openxla/xla/issues/49120#issuecomment-5794234275","id":5794234275,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/49120","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOHyx1PM8AAAABWVz_ow","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5794234275/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-09-23T11:46:54Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openxla/xla/issues/comments/5794234275","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14309772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/akuegel","id":14309772,"login":"akuegel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzA5Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akuegel","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Summary\n\nA `dynamic-update-slice` with constant, out-of-range start indices is lowered on GPU through the dynamic-slice copy path, whose recorded `byte_offset` is computed from the raw starts. `DynamicUpdateSlice` semantics clamp each start into `[0, dim − update_dim]`; the copy path skips that, so the update is written at the wrong offset. Hence, the target window keeps stale values and the tail lands in the next row. \n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nimport os; os.environ.setdefault(\"XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE\", \"false\")\nimport numpy as np, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\nshape = (3, 127, 1, 33)\nx = (np.arange(int(np.prod(shape)), dtype=np.int64).reshape(shape) * 7919 % 10007 - 5000).astype(np.int32)\n\ndef f(x):\n    t = x[:, 94]                                                 # static slice -> (3, 1, 33)\n    upd = lax.dynamic_slice(t, [0, 0, 0], (1, 1, 8)) * 3 - 1      # update derived from the operand\n    return lax.dynamic_update_slice(t, upd, [1, 1, 31])         # start (1, 1, 31) clamps to (1, 0, 25)\n\nt = x[:, 94]; ref = t.copy(); ref[1, 0, 25:33] = t[0, 0, 0:8] * 3 - 1\nfor dev in {d.platform: d for d in jax.devices() + jax.devices(\"cpu\")}.values():\n    with jax.default_device(dev):\n        out = np.asarray(jax.jit(f)(jnp.asarray(x)))\n    bad = np.argwhere(out != ref)\n    print(f\"{dev.platform}: \" + (\"ok\" if bad.size == 0 else f\"WRONG {bad.shape[0]} elements; positions {[b.tolist() for b in bad]}\"))\n```\n\n```\ngpu: WRONG 14 elements; positions [[1,0,25] … [1,0,32], [2,0,0] … [2,0,5]]\ncpu: ok\n```\n\n## Agent Analysis \n\n## Analysis\n\nIn the dump after `dynamic-slice-annotator` the DUS carries\n`\"dynamic_slice_config\":{\"byte_offset\":\"256\",\"byte_stride\":\"0\"}`: 256 B = 64 elements = `1·33 + 31`, the linearization of the unclamped starts; the clamped starts `(1, 0, 25)` give 58. `dynamic_slice_fusion_v2_thunk.cc` then applies only `ClampSliceOffset` against the whole buffer (`[0, buffer_size − slice_size]`), which 256 B passes. The per-dimension clamp is applied nowhere on this path; the regular loop emitter (used for traced starts and on CPU) clamps correctly. Relevant code: `dynamic_slice_analysis.cc` (`AnalyzeDynamicSlice`, byte offset from constant starts), `dynamic_slice_annotator.cc`, `dynamic_slice_fusion_v2_thunk.cc`. The path landed with PR #44044 (June 2026).\n","clo